Sure, the map() method in Java 8 Stream API is a very powerful tool that can be used for a variety of tasks. Here are some examples:

Type Conversion: You can use map() to convert each element in the stream from one type to another1. For example, you can convert a Stream<String> to a Stream<Integer>:
Java

List<String> strings = Arrays.asList("1", "2", "3");
List<Integer> integers = strings.stream()
    .map(Integer::valueOf)
    .collect(Collectors.toList());
